    "id": "q18",
    "topic": "Collapse all questions",
    "questionText": "Family, from State A, was in the process of moving into their new home in State A when an issue with the plumbing caused the home to become temporarily uninhabitable. While the family hired a certified plumbing company to rectify the issue, the family moved into a hotel suite in State B but only miles from their new home. During their hotel stay, a diversity action was filed against the parents relating to a car accident they had been involved in two years prior. While the family was visiting the local zoo, a process server went to the hotel where the family was staying and left the paperwork with the hotel housekeeping staff with the explicit instruction to hand deliver the envelope to the parents upon their return to their room. Knowing that the parents made coffee every morning, the housekeeping staff left the envelope on top of the room\u2019s coffee machine. As soon as the family returned from their day trip that same evening, the parents saw and opened the envelope. The following week, the parents filed a motion to dismiss. How should the court rule on the motion?",
