    "id": "q7",
    "topic": "Collapse all questions",
    "questionText": "Guest filed suit against Homeowner, alleging the Homeowner maintained a dangerous condition in his home causing the Guest to trip and fall during a holiday party. The allegations stemmed from a loose floorboard in the Homeowner\u2019s living room, in which the Guest tripped over while dancing. After a trial on the merits, the jury found for the Guest. Shortly thereafter, the Homeowner brought suit against Guest, alleging that Guest refused to heed the Homeowner\u2019s warnings of the loose floorboard and that she destroyed a priceless antique vase when she fell. After filing her Answer with all applicable defenses, the Guest filed a motion for summary judgment on the vase claim. How should the court rule on the motion?",
